@startuml sequence-restoration-review
!include ../../../tools/diagrams/elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: the human-in-the-loop path. An operator opens a flagged book in the
'       page studio (deep-zoom tiles over IIIF), fixes a disputed region (draws
'       or relabels a rectangle: stamp, table, figure, formula…), adds a note or
'       a page override, and re-runs just that page on the priority queue; the
'       result streams back over SSE. Every confirmed region is also stored as a
'       labelled training example. Approving the book rebuilds its outputs and
'       publishes (or republishes) it to the catalog (dev now, prod later) in place: the
'       entry is created or updated and its acquisitions point at the digitized
'       tree (external_url), the publication row keeps the entry id and version.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one review session, proposal. Scope: the operator
'       request/response, job and event flow. Omitted: tile generation details,
'       telemetry, catalog authentication (API key), PDF/A validation.
' Source: design session 2026-11-07 (review only when flagged, feedback = re-run
'         affected pages + training data export, prod publish in place);
'         Cookbooks/Digitalizer.md §6 (import contract, 409 handling) and §8
'         (external_url), 2026-11-06.
' Render: python3 tools/diagrams/render.py vault/evilflowers-knowledge/Diagrams/sequence-restoration-review.puml
' =============================================================================

title Operator review: fix a disputed region, re-run one page, approve, republish (proposal, 2026-11-07)

actor "**Operator**\nSPA page studio" as op
participant "**studio-api**\nFastAPI" as api <<focus>>
database "**postgresql18**\ndb digitalizer" as pg
queue "**redis**\nqueues · pub/sub" as redis
participant "**worker-cpu**\nqueues interactive, cpu" as wcpu
participant "**worker-io**" as wio
participant "**NFS** · gateway\ndigitized/studio/" as nfs
participant "**evilflowers** catalog\nREST /api/v1\n(dev now, prod later)" as cat

op -> api : GET /books/{id} (pages, regions, disputes, notes)
api -> pg : read book
api --> op : JSON
op -> api : GET /iiif/{page}/… (deep-zoom tiles)
api -> nfs : read tile
api --> op : tiles (immutable, cached)
op -> api : GET /events?book={id} (SSE, stays open)

== fix one disputed region ==
op -> api : PATCH /regions/{r} {kind: stamp, action: remove}\n+ note "library seal, not content"
api -> pg : region confirmed (source operator)\n+ training example (DocLayNet label)
op -[$accent_msg()]-> api : <b>POST /books/{id}/reruns {pages: [12]}</b>
api -> pg : run (pages 12, overrides pinned)
api -> redis : enqueue page 12 (priority: interactive)
api --> op : 202 + run id
redis -> wcpu : process page 12 (jumps the bulk backlog)
wcpu -> nfs : re-clean · re-OCR · new tiles + page render
wcpu -> pg : page version 2, disputes resolved
wcpu -> redis : publish page.updated
redis --> api : event
api -[$accent_msg()]-> op : <b>SSE page.updated → studio swaps the tile</b>

== approve and publish ==
op -> api : POST /books/{id}/approve {operator: "jana"}
api -> pg : review decision (who, when, notes)
api -> redis : enqueue rebuild + publish
redis -> wcpu : rebuild PDF · PDF/A-2b · EPUB
wcpu -> nfs : write digitized/studio/<project>/<item_id>/…
redis -> wio : publish
wio -> pg : read publication (entry id, version)
alt first publication
  wio -> cat : POST /entries (title, authors, ISBN…)
  cat --> wio : 201 entry id
else republish
  wio -> cat : PUT /entries/{id} (corrected metadata)
end
wio -> cat : acquisitions: external_url →\nhttps://elvira.stuba.sk/digitized/<project>/<item_id>/….pdf, .epub
cat --> wio : 200
wio -> pg : publication v(n+1), entry id
wio -> redis : publish book.published
redis --> api : event
api --> op : SSE book.published (v2)

caption An operator decision never waits for the bulk backlog: re-runs go to an interactive priority queue, and the page studio swaps\nthe tile when the SSE event arrives. Republishing is idempotent through the stored entry id; files are served in place\n(external_url), so a republish only swaps files on the volume and updates the entry, never re-uploads gigabytes.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-knowledge · Diagrams/sequence-restoration-review.puml
@enduml
